00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:47.130
That sounds like a menu for
a sushi restaurant, not a Japanese-style café.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.740
The concept will be a 
café where you can eat

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.360
the season's freshest seafood

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.590
along with the best sake, 
hand-picked by the owner.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:59.260
That's a sushi restaurant
not a café, right?

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.000
No, it's not. Also,

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.480
in the middle of the café, 
there'll be an aquarium.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.520
There'll be fish swimming around in it

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.520
and customers can choose which 
fish they want to eat.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.630
There aren't any cafés 
with fish tanks.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.340
You need something a café would have.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.970
Something a café would have?
You don't get it?

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.550
It's Penguin's <i>Café</i>.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:23.400
That's just the name.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:27.010
Then, why don't you try serving coffee?

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:30.160
Well, I'd be busy getting the 
fish from the fish market.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.260
I don't know if I'd be able 
to handle coffee, too.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.510
You might as well hang up the café idea.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:36.690
What are you talking about?!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:37.930
I'm totally going to do it!

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:47.900
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.320
Welcome!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.240
CAFÉ

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.850
Sir, what can I get'cha?

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.080
Change everything back.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.910
How about Llama's Café?

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.260
What kind of café is it?

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.370
It's a café with llamas in it.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.090
Well, that's original.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.710
Would you be able to carry the coffee?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.670
It would all depend on balance.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.150
As for the concept,

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.400
it'll be a café where you can 
feed the llamas grass,

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.310
groom them, and adore them freely.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.890
It's like a Cat Café.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.000
You can groom the llamas.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.610
Isn't that amazing?

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.610
I don't know. Is that actually fun?

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.110
Not only that,

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:41.750
you can pick your favorite llama

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.320
and take them outside for a walk.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.070
<i>I'll take this llama.</i>

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.870
<i>Thank you, sir.</i>

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.050
<i>Do you want to stop to eat some grass?</i>

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:08.890
Hokkyo kugen

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:08.890
Ramen
Gyoza

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.780
<i>It needs a bit of salt.</i>

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.940
Doesn't it sound wonderful?

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.440
I'm having a hard time 
thinking that'd be fun.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:18.350
Panda's Café is the best, 
without a doubt.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.950
Don't you mean Penguin's Café?

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:23.720
Hey, what do you think, Polar Bear?

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:28.660
Llama's Café.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:30.280
I told you.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.490
What about you, Miss Sasako?

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.170
Hm?

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.130
Which café do you think is the best?

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.190
Let's see...

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:41.590
How about Sasako's Café?

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.530
I'm telling you, it's all 
about Panda's Café.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.890
What? Surely you mean Penguin's Café.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.670
No, no, it's Llama's Café.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.770
H-Hey!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.930
Please listen!

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:58.680
What would it be like?

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.820
Well, let's see...

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.320
There's a panda-like 
Miss Sasako, right?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:06.350
Then that wouldn't be any 
different from Panda's Café.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.420
No, no. There's a llama-like 
Miss Sasako and...

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.920
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:14.310
The Café's Cherry Blossom Viewing Party!

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.380
Don't tell anyone.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:18.750
All right.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:23.760
I have a penguin that I like.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.760
Excuse me. Could I get 
a green tea parfait?

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.180
And?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.190
I have a penguin that I like—

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:38.250
Excuse me, could you change 
that to a strawberry parfait?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.490
Hey! Are you even listening?!

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:42.420
Hello!

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.700
Could I get the usual, Polar Bear?

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:49.580
There you go.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.560
A large serving of bamboo.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:55.510
Thanks for the meal!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:04.640
Should we do it?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:06.890
What?

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.490
A cherry blossom viewing party.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.500
Look at those cherry blossoms!

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.280
Aren't they beautiful?

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.780
Let's go over there.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.200
It's amazing.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.740
They blossomed amazingly 
again this year.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:34.550
I wonder what we should 
do for snacks...

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:36.190
What an unromantic thing to say.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:39.220
We're talking about how pretty 
the cherry blossoms are.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.850
Hey, do you have any snacks?

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.570
You're not listening at all.

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:45.710
Oh, well.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.450
I wonder if the cherry 
blossoms are edible.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.680
And another one who doesn't get it.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.230
You probably could, 
considering you eat grass, as well.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.270
Hey, do you have any bamboo?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.730
No.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.540
I packed a lunch for us.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.400
You're amazing, Polar Bear!

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:12.700
I'm... going to... run some errands...

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.010
Sloth?

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.740
I'm going... to buy...

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:21.930
a drink... at the... 
convenience store—

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:24.280
It's all right, we have enough here.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:28.250
It's just right over there...

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.300
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.350
I'll be... right back...

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.810
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.000
Bye, now...

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.420
See ya.

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.190
Cheers!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.040
This is great!

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:03.420
They're so beautiful, 
but they fall so quickly.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.910
It's all so fleeting.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.640
This is a new recipe I tried.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:12.040
Oh! It looks delicious!

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.670
Thank you for the food!

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.570
Hey! Stop eating and 
let's do something

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:25.110
more fitting for a cherry 
blossom viewing party.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.780
More fitting for a cherry 
blossom viewing party?

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.030
Like singing.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.490
I'm terrible at singing.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:38.950
Same here.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.410
I am, as well.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.380
How about dancing?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.050
Dance?

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.550
We're going to dance?

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:50.470
Dancing, you say?

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:54.990
Hula dancing?

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.560
Belly dancing?

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:01.780
Stomach dancing?

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.300
Mr. Penguin is sleeping.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.080
That's not it!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.990
I'm just got tired of your 
stupid puns and fell over!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:13.570
Well, that was rude, Mr. Penguin.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.740
You know there's more 
to do at these events!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.400
How about impersonations?!

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.750
That's totally an impersonation 
of Mr. Nagura!

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:27.290
I'm just... eating.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.920
We're lacking something.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.680
I know! Polar Bear!

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.260
Lift me up to that tree there!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.990
I'll fly!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:38.220
I don't think that's a good idea.

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.870
Why are you trying to stop me?!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.940
Then you do it, Panda!

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:46.880
Come on! Lift me up into the tree!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.150
I'm Llama.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.970
He appears to be rather drunk.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.320
I think he drank too much.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:17:02.330
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.150
Wow, that's amazing!

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:18.050
It's like a real cherry 
blossom viewing party!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.300
Mr. Penguin?

00:17:24.530 --> 00:17:25.900
He's asleep.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.120
He's totally knocked out.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:31.590
Hey! Don't sleep!

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:32.740
We're awake.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:38.060
Young penguins these days
 just don't get it!

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.750
It's not just about being cute!

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.200
Am I right?!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.160
Now he's picking fights.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.800
Are you listening, Mr. Yoshizaki?!

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:48.350
Who's that?

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:51.640
Oh no! You have bruises around 
your eyes, Mr. Yoshizaki!

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.240
Did someone hit you?

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:54.980
Are you okay?!

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.430
This is getting annoying.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.220
Hey, Mr. Nagura. Are you listening?

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.890
I'm just... eating.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:07.350
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:12.230
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:14.430
What?

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.760
I have a penguin that I like.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:21.020
Her name is Miss Penko and she 
works at the bakery part-time.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.660
Miss Penko!

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:27.250
I'm Panda!

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.460
Please share the same fish with me

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.320
for as long as we both live, Miss Penko!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.360
Please!

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.500
Help me!

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:39.220
This is rather amusing, so I'll just watch.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.970
Jeez!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.570
W-Will you listen to 
what I have to say?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:43.920
What?

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:47.250
I wrote a poem about Miss Penko.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.190
Really? How does it go?

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.610
"The Miss Penko"

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.400
"The"?

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.790
"Miss Penko laughs.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.280
Miss Penko walks.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.590
Miss Penko eats fish."

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.120
What do you think, Miss Penko?

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.550
Me?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:16.110
Why don't you go on a walk with 
Miss Penko, Mr. Penguin?

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:17.550
Wow, really?!

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:20.550
Let's go, Miss Penko.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:23.040
Why is it me again?

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.260
Come on, let's go.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:29.660
It'll be a romantic evening 
with just the two of us.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:33.190
I can't help but feel there's 
a lot wrong with this.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.900
I wish we could walk like this forever.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.280
I want to go home.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:43.500
Miss Penko, will you 
go out with—  What?!

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.470
Where did you come 
from, Mr. Yoshizaki?!

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:47.690
Who is Mr. Yoshizaki?

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:49.250
Miss Penko, where did you go?!

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.860
Miss Penko!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.460
Mr. Penguin!

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.720
He's asleep.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.720
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.830
I'm back...

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:37.860
I went... to the convenience store...

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:44.330
No one's... here...

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:49.010
The night blossoms are pretty, too.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.110
Yesterday was pretty crazy.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.630
It's like that every year.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:31.520
Mr. Penguin doesn't handle 
 alcohol very well.

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:35.570
Hello.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:38.480
My head is pounding for some reason.

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:43.400
Oh, did you buy that from the 
bakery Miss Penko works at?

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:46.950
What?! How do you know about that?!

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:49.370
"The Miss Penko"

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.330
How do you know about my poem?!

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.120
Why do you know about it?!

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:57.120
"Please share the same fish with me

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.080
for as long as we both live, Miss Penko!"

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:03.300
The words I was going to 
use for my proposal!

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:05.700
How do you know about that?!

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:08.260
You don't remember?

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.780
I-I haven't even told anyone!

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:14.110
"Miss Penko laughs."

00:22:14.110 --> 00:22:16.180
"Miss Penko walks."

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:18.630
"Miss Penko eats fish."

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.630
Knock it off!

00:23:54.930 --> 00:24:06.650
Please stay outside
the fence.

00:23:54.930 --> 00:24:24.520
Next Time

00:23:57.020 --> 00:23:59.040
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.450
Did you have some 
plastic surgery done?

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:01.560
No, I didn't.

00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:04.420
But let me ask, why did you think that?

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:09.470
But now let me ask, what do you think 
<i>nata de coco</i> is made from?

00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:12.160
Please stay outside
the fence.

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:11.210
How did you think to ask that?

00:24:11.210 --> 00:24:13.390
Could you wrap this up, Polar Bear?

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:16.280
Please stay outside
the fence.

00:24:14.570 --> 00:24:16.260
The next <i>Polar Bear's Café</i>

00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:18.530
will be presented in live-action.

00:24:18.530 --> 00:24:19.480
Enjoy!

00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:20.610
No, it won't!

00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:24.520
Polar Bear at the Zoo
Panda's Anguish{Z: TLC please. Added these myself.}

00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:21.780
It'll be animated.

00:24:21.780 --> 00:24:23.130
Enjoy!
